/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In the gas film the driving force is y − yi; in the liquid film it is xi − x.
   - Add the two film drops on the gas basis.
   - Ky is the overall gas coefficient, kmol/(m²·s); ky is the gas-film coefficient, kmol/(m²·s); kx is the liquid-film coefficient, kmol/(m²·s); m is the slope of y* = m x, dimensionless.
   - On the liquid basis, x* − xi = (y − yi)/m = NA/(m ky) and xi − x = NA/kx.
   - Kx is the overall liquid coefficient, kmol/(m²·s); the gas term 1/(m ky) converts gas-film resistance to the x basis; the liquid term 1/kx is the liquid-film resistance.
   - The factor m converts one phase's composition to the other phase's basis.
   - When the equilibrium line is curved, m in 1/Ky = 1/ky + m/kx is the slope m′ of the chord from (x, y*) to (xi, yi), and m in 1/Kx is the slope m″ of the chord from (xi, yi) to (x*, y).
   - Resistance is 1/coefficient.
*/
